<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Troezen Decree</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Decree of Themistocles</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Troezen Decree is a marble inscription found at Troezen in 1959 and published by Michael Jameson in 1960. Carved in the 3rd century BCE, it claims to reproduce the decree proposed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/themistocles">Themistocles</a> in 480 BCE ordering the evacuation of Athenian women and children to Troezen and the manning of the fleet before the battle of Salamis. Whether it preserves an authentic text or a later reconstruction is still debated.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/troezen-decree.jpg" alt="Troezen Decree" width="320" height="487" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artistUnknown artist · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:EPMA-13330-Themistocle_decree-2.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
